bilbo keeps durable memory for coding agents: it remembers their sessions and
the pages they cite, and recalls them when a later session asks.

[1mUsage:[22m bilbo <verb> [<args>]...

[1mKeep:[22m
  [1mremember[22m  Keep files as entries; a later run keeps what grew or changed

[1mSettings:[22m
  [1mconfig[22m    Show each setting, its value and where the value came from

[1mExit codes:[22m 0 success; 1 refused, problems found or nothing matched; 2 usage
or config error.
Results go to stdout; diagnostics to stderr, prefixed 'bilbo: ' off a terminal.

[1mPaths, the first that applies:[22m
  [1mroot[22m    $BILBO_HOME, paths.root, $XDG_DATA_HOME/bilbo, ~/.local/share/bilbo
  [1mconfig[22m  $BILBO_CONFIG, $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/bilbo/config.toml,
          ~/.config/bilbo/config.toml
  [1mcache[22m   paths.cache, $XDG_CACHE_HOME/bilbo, ~/.cache/bilbo
  [1mstate[22m   paths.state, $XDG_STATE_HOME/bilbo, ~/.local/state/bilbo
'bilbo config' shows every setting; reference/configuration.md says what each
one means.

Run 'bilbo <verb> --help' or 'bilbo help <verb>' for a verb's options, output
and exit codes.
